    "finalName": "",
    "description": "You can use a ranged weapon as a melee weapon without taking a penalty on your attack roll. The weapon is otherwise treated as a <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Club\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Club\">Club</a> in all respects.<br><br>If you are using a <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Rifle\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Rifle\">Rifle</a> with a mounted <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Bayonet\" title=\"Bayonet\">Bayonet</a> or <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Vibrobayonet\" title=\"Vibrobayonet\">Vibrobayonet</a>, you may wield that weapon as a Double Weapon. The <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Bayonet\" title=\"Bayonet\">Bayonet</a> or <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Vibrobayonet\" title=\"Vibrobayonet\">Vibrobayonet</a> end is treated normally, and the other end is treated as a <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Club\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Club\">Club</a>.",
